<p>
  {dgettext("help_commands", "Remove a ban from a user, allowing them to rejoin the channel.")}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_question}>{dgettext("help_commands", "When to Use It")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Use it when a ban has served its purpose, or when someone was banned by mistake."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_code}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Syntax")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/unban <nickname>")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tag}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Parameters")}</.help_h4>
<p><code>nickname</code> {dgettext("help_commands", "— The user to unban.")}</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_commands", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Removes the ban entry for the specified user. Once unbanned, the user can rejoin the channel normally. For registered channels, the unban is persisted. You can also unban using"
  )} <code>{dgettext("help_commands", "/mode -b nickname")}</code>.
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "The command acts on the channel you are viewing. Everyone in the channel sees a line that names the user and who lifted the ban. Unbanning does not invite the user or bring them back. They must join again themselves."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "The name must match the ban entry exactly, with the same upper and lower case. A ban set as a wildcard mask, such as %{mask}, is removed only by typing that same mask. If no ban entry matches, the command still reports the unban and nothing changes.",
    mask: "Troll*"
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Rules & Limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Requires channel operator or owner status")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Half-operators cannot use this command")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "You must type it in a channel window, not in a private conversation"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Without a nickname, you see the usage line")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Only the first nickname is used. Extra words are ignored.")}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Examples")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/unban user123")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_commands", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-ban">{dgettext("help_commands", "/ban")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-kick">{dgettext("help_commands", "/kick")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-mode">{dgettext("help_commands", "/mode")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-ban-exceptions">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Ban Exceptions (+e)")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-permissions">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Channel Permissions")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-channel-central">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Channel Central")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
